\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces  Error envelopes for the energy spectrum as a result of oscillation parameters. 10k\nobreakspace  {}toy MC experiments were generated with randomized systematic parameters and the 1$\sigma $ spread of bin contents was calculated. BANFF tuned MC templates were used. Existing correlations between the systematic parameters were taken into account. The $\mathaccentV {bar}016{\nu }_{\mu } \to \mathaccentV {bar}016{\nu }_e$ signal is disabled setting $\beta =0$. The error envelopes in each bin correspond to the $1\sigma $ error obtained from the distribution of the extracted number of events. First the median is found. Then the upper (lower) error corresponds to the number of events for which the 34\% of toys is contained in the right (left) side of the median. The continuos line shows the expected nominal reconstructed energy distribution for pre-BANFF (blue) and post-BANFF (black). \relax }}{24}{figure.caption.16}}
