\newlabel{fig:RHC1Re_oscillated_all_envelope_ratio}{{27}{29}{Error envelopes, expressed as a ratio of event count, for the energy spectrum as a result of all systematic parameters. \NumToys toy MC experiments were generated with randomized systematic parameters and the 1$\sigma $ spread of bin contents was calculated. BANFF tuned MC templates were used. All systematic parameters were considered and their correlations were taken into account. Oscillations were applied with the parameter values shown in table~\ref {tab:osc_params_fixed_values_reactor}. The fractional error in each bin corresponds to the $1\sigma $ error obtained from the distribution of the extracted number of events. First the median (red line) is found. Then the upper (lower) error corresponds to the number of events for which the 34\% of toys is contained in the right (left) side of the median. The continuos line shows the pre-BANFF (blue) and post-BANFF (red) ratios. \relax }{figure.caption.23}{}}
