\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {38}{\ignorespaces  Predicted reconstructed-energy spectrum components of 1 $e$-like ring events from various true neutrino reaction modes, in antineutrino beam mode with oscillations. The following components are shown separately: $\mathaccentV {bar}016{\nu }_{\mu } \to \mathaccentV {bar}016{\nu }_e$ signal (green), $\nu _{\mu } \to \nu _e$ background (grey), NC (red) background, background other (blue) and all background components. The spectrum was generated using the BANFF postfit MC templates. Each component is separately shown. The spectrum shown was generated assuming the normal hierarchy and the oscillation parameters in table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:osc_params_fixed_values_reactor}. The black dots correspond to Run 5+6 dataset (4.0108$\times $10$^{20}$POT). On the left plot each component is first normalized to 4.0108$\times $10$^{20}$POT and then rescaled of a factor 7 in order to better compare with data. On the right plot each component is first normalized to its area and then rescaled by a factor 7. \relax }}{39}{figure.caption.43}}
