\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {46}{\ignorespaces  Reconstructed energy distribution obtained by making 10k\nobreakspace  {}toys where only the MEC oxygen parameter is randomly extracted and all the other systematic parameters are fixed to the nominal values. The red line correspond to the Asimov dataset where the MEC parameter is fixed to its nominal value. The error envelopes in each bin correspond to the $1\sigma $ error obtained from the distribution of the extracted number of events. First the median (red line) is found. Then the upper (lower) error corresponds to the number of events for which the 34\% of toys is contained between it and the median on the right (left) side. The black line shows the expected nominal reconstructed energy distribution. Pre-BANFF is shown on the left, while post-BANF is shown on the right. \relax }}{48}{figure.caption.55}}
\newlabel{fig:mec_error_envelope}{{46}{48}{Reconstructed energy distribution obtained by making \NumToys toys where only the MEC oxygen parameter is randomly extracted and all the other systematic parameters are fixed to the nominal values. The red line correspond to the Asimov dataset where the MEC parameter is fixed to its nominal value. The error envelopes in each bin correspond to the $1\sigma $ error obtained from the distribution of the extracted number of events. First the median (red line) is found. Then the upper (lower) error corresponds to the number of events for which the 34\% of toys is contained between it and the median on the right (left) side. The black line shows the expected nominal reconstructed energy distribution. Pre-BANFF is shown on the left, while post-BANF is shown on the right. \relax }{figure.caption.55}{}}
